<!--
  Hub studio · `/studio/agents/:id` — the single-agent detail viewer.

  Composes the `@ship/agents` pack's <ship-agent-detail>, passing
  the route's `[id]` param as the composite's `id` prop. The
  composite owns the data wiring (ship.agents.detail({ id }) via
  live() inside the controller) and renders the agent's identity
  header, description, tags, capabilities, and source path.

  The route is a thin composition — chrome is the root layout, the
  page body is the pack composite + the `id` prop binding.

  Top chrome: the <ship-nav-top> is owned by the root layout
  (`routes/_layout.sui` → `<ship-app-chrome>`).

  Per the hub-buildout-charter §Connect-only, the detail is wired to
  the real Connect SDK op `ship.agents.detail({ id })`. The composite's
  controller narrows the `unknown` payload to the per-agent shape
  the surface renders; missing fields fall back to the id-hash hue
  and the id-derived initials.
-->
<main class="studio-agent-detail">
  <ship-agent-detail prop:id={id()}></ship-agent-detail>
</main>
